<sect1 id="namespacecsmp_1implementation">
<title>Implementation</title><para><orderedlist>
<listitem><para>test whether at least one element node is overpressured.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>only where an overpressure exists conductivity shall be diffused.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>back calculating dP/dxy from transport velocity.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>the conductivity is enhanced propertional to pressure gradient over the storativity, since = dQ / bc.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>calculating desired flux in element with bc as the proportionality constant between desired pressure change and flux.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>calculating conductivity needed to accomodate this flux. This makes sense only where there is an appreciable pressure gradient. Otherwise an increased conductivity will not foster the flow. <linebreak/>
</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>only if the new conductivity is greater than the old one it is assigned. </para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
</sect1>
